// A program's own call of Preload's __runtime_error (issue #157, spec 8.1)
// with an empty text: it stops the program as a failing check does, exit
// status 101, and writes its text, which is nothing, so stderr is empty.
// Interpreted, the same (spec 10.8): the text as given, not a line made up
// from where the call is.
#import "Basic";

main :: () {
    print_line("before");
    __runtime_error("", 0);
    print_line("not reached");
}
